# UST.G3CA Selected Delta-Correction H02 Source

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_SELECTED_H02_SOURCE_CLASS_AND_ONE_SPLIT_PRIME_COORDINATES`

## Theorem

Let `C_section` be the 19-term G3BI deformation section obtained from the
stored Cayley correction `s*C_section` by removing its single Cayley factor.
With the normalized q79 splitting-conic polynomial `P_delta`, form

```text
S_delta = u*v*P_delta*(t0*t1*t2)*C_section.
```

The factors have Cox degrees

```text
deg(u*v*t0*t1*t2) = (0,0,2),
deg(P_delta*C_section) = (9,1,0),
```

and direct termwise collection proves that every monomial of `S_delta` has
Cox degree `(9,1,2)`. The exact representative has 100 nonzero monomials over
`Q(gamma)` and lies in the frozen H02 Macaulay ambient basis.

Reduce this representative through the selected corrected G3BI endpoint
chart modulo `21,817`. At all six roots

```text
5, 1971, 6912, 10062, 10605, 14055
```

of the selected sextic, the `42,706`-row sparse solve has zero residual. Each
solution emits a nonzero, in fact dense, 248-coordinate B103 H02 quotient
vector. Lagrange interpolation across the six roots gives a complete
`248 x 6` power-basis tensor modulo `21,817`; all 1,488 entries are nonzero,
and evaluating the tensor back at every root reproduces the six solved
vectors exactly.

Consequently `S_delta` is a nonzero characteristic-zero H02 source class for
the selected correction direction, and its full B103 quotient-coordinate
reduction is known at one completely split good prime.

## Source Typing

The distinction between `C_section` and `s*C_section` is essential. G3BI
stores the full Cayley correction `s*C_section`, while the affine-source
formula uses the deformation section `dot F`, hence `C_section` before the
path scalar is applied. Inserting the Cayley `s` a second time would change
the Cox degree from `(9,1,2)` to `(0,0,3)` and would not define the H02 class
proved here.

Along G3BJ,

```text
F(a) = F_B89 + a*C_section,
a(t) = 1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t),
dot F(t) = a'(t)*C_section.
```

G3CA calculates the unscaled source associated with `C_section`; continuation
to a path point supplies the scalar `a'(t)`.

## Consequence

The immediate source ambiguity is removed. G3BZ supplies the exact
rank-6,022 selected path update, while G3CA supplies the actual one-vector
H02 source on which that update must act. The next operator calculation is
therefore a selected one-source resolvent/continuation problem, not a search
over arbitrary H02 derivative columns.

## Boundary

This theorem does not reconstruct the 248 coordinates over `Q(gamma)`,
produce a flat rank-1,509 relative-de-Rham lift along the full G3BJ path,
identify the spectral trace-test row order with B103 coordinates, perform
integral Gauss-Manin transport, or decide `beta_C`. Those remain separate
promotion and frame-binding obligations.

